                          "text":  "I am the last one. The third Moon car, on the final Apollo landing, in December 1972.\n\nMy drivers were Gene Cernan and Jack Schmitt. Jack was a geologist, the first professional scientist to walk on the Moon, and he wanted to see everything. So we drove about 36 kilometres through the Taurus-Littrow valley. At one point we were more than 7 kilometres from the lander.",
